    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, **James Wood** (75.97) stands as our premier offensive anchor, fueled by an elite 0.426 xwOBA and a juicy matchup against Bratt, whose 5.90 xERA offers a massive ceiling for production. While **Brice Turang** (72.70) and **Tyler Soderstrom** (72.72) sit just behind in raw efficiency, their favorable pairings against Feltner and Paredes respectively\u2014both of whom provide significant SP skill advantages\u2014make them core targets for counting stats today. **Austin Riley** (72.42) also warrants attention; despite the lower-order placement, his projected 16% park factor bump against Young creates a rare opportunity for high-leverage power production that our model couldn't ignore. \n\nThe decision-making process was most difficult regarding **Isaac Paredes**, who logged a solid 52.31 but ultimately fell to the bench. While his platoon edge against Burke offered a potential floor, the optimizer prioritized the higher projected efficiency and category-specific utility of **Gabriel Moreno** and **Josh Naylor**. We are also closely monitoring the risks inherent in **Seiya Suzuki**\u2019s start (45.36); facing the formidable Skenes is a distinct \"below floor\" danger zone, and his sub-50 score is buoyed almost entirely by his position in the two-hole. Similarly, **Jose Caballero** remains a high-variance play; while his 51.18 score reflects his importance to our SB strategy, he faces an elite catcher who threatens to stifle our stolen base upside. We remain wary of these \"marginal\" starts but will ride the high-speed profiles of **Corbin Carroll** and **James Wood** to mitigate the damage against tough arms like Skenes and Griffin.",
